note SemC catalog v1 (seed/catalog). Each entry is a record: its `note card` and `note eg` lines and
note the fn block that follows them. identity = sha256 of the record bytes (resolve ids catalog.om).
note Only the fn block is copied into a unit. Admitted subset and limits: README.md.

note card adds k to x exactly n times in a for loop; overflow traps like add; n <= 1000000
note eg ret add_times x 4 3
fn add_times x int k int n ulong to int
s = x
for i ulong n
s = add s k
end
ret s
end
